      "math_academy_id": "e-3629",
      "problem": "Given that $y=4\\log_3 x,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we apply our formula for the derivative when the base of the logarithm is a number other than $e.$ By doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}&=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x \\ln 3}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{4}{x \\ln 3}.\n\n}\n$$",
